    },
    "excluded_steps": [],
    "format_errors": [],
    "steps": [
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 69,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 71,
        "char_start": 0,
        "effective_step": 1,
        "end_token_index": 26,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 27,
        "step_number": 1,
        "text": "Step 1: Let \\( \\angle BAC = \\theta \\). Then \\( \\angle BDC = 3\\theta \\)."
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 198,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 200,
        "char_start": 73,
        "effective_step": 2,
        "end_token_index": 74,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 75,
        "step_number": 2,
        "text": "Step 2: Since \\( AB = AC \\), triangle \\( ABC \\) is isosceles with \\( \\angle ABC = \\angle ACB = \\frac{180^\\circ - \\theta}{2} \\)."
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 332,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 334,
        "char_start": 202,
        "effective_step": 3,
        "end_token_index": 129,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 130,
        "step_number": 3,
        "text": "Step 3: In triangle \\( BDC \\), we have \\( \\angle BDC = 3\\theta \\) and \\( \\angle DBC = \\angle DCB = \\frac{180^\\circ - 3\\theta}{2} \\)."
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 445,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 447,
        "char_start": 336,
        "effective_step": 4,
        "end_token_index": 165,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 166,
        "step_number": 4,
        "text": "Step 4: Using the fact that \\( AM \\) is the altitude, we know \\( \\angle BAM = \\angle CAM = \\frac{\\theta}{2} \\)."
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 536,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 538,
        "char_start": 449,
        "effective_step": 5,
        "end_token_index": 200,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 201,
        "step_number": 5,
        "text": "Step 5: Consider triangle \\( ADM \\). Since \\( AD = 10 \\) and \\( AM = 11 \\), \\( DM = 1 \\)."
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 922,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 923,
        "char_start": 540,
        "effective_step": 6,
        "end_token_index": 368,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 369,
        "step_number": 6,
        "text": "Step 6: Apply the Law of Sines in triangle \\( BDM \\):\n\\[ \\frac{BD}{\\sin \\angle DMB} = \\frac{DM}{\\sin \\angle DBM} \\]\nSince \\( \\angle DMB = 180^\\circ - 3\\theta \\) and \\( \\angle DBM = \\frac{180^\\circ - 3\\theta}{2} \\), we get:\n\\[ \\frac{BD}{\\sin (180^\\circ - 3\\theta)} = \\frac{1}{\\sin \\left(\\frac{180^\\circ - 3\\theta}{2}\\right)} \\]\n\\[ BD = \\frac{1}{\\sin \\left(\\frac{3\\theta}{2}\\right)} \\]"
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 1200,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 1201,
        "char_start": 925,
        "effective_step": 7,
        "end_token_index": 481,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 482,
        "step_number": 7,
        "text": "Step 7: Apply the Law of Sines in triangle \\( BDM \\) again for triangle \\( BDM \\) and \\( CMD \\):\n\\[ \\frac{BD}{\\sin \\left(\\frac{180^\\circ - 3\\theta}{2}\\right)} = \\frac{BM}{\\sin 3\\theta} \\]\n\\[ BM = \\frac{BD \\cdot \\sin 3\\theta}{\\sin \\left(\\frac{180^\\circ - 3\\theta}{2}\\right)} \\]"
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 1307,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 1309,
        "char_start": 1203,
        "effective_step": 8,
        "end_token_index": 521,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 522,
        "step_number": 8,
        "text": "Step 8: Use the identity \\( \\sin 3\\theta = 3\\sin \\theta - 4\\sin^3 \\theta \\) and simplify to find \\( BM \\)."
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 1487,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 1488,
        "char_start": 1311,
        "effective_step": 9,
        "end_token_index": 591,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 592,
        "step_number": 9,
        "text": "Step 9: Since \\( BM = CM \\) and \\( BM + CM = BC \\), we can use the Pythagorean theorem in triangle \\( ABM \\) to find \\( AB \\):\n\\[ AB = \\sqrt{AM^2 + BM^2} = \\sqrt{11^2 + BM^2} \\]"
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 1593,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 1595,
        "char_start": 1490,
        "effective_step": 10,
        "end_token_index": 621,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 622,
        "step_number": 10,
        "text": "Step 10: After solving the trigonometric equations and simplifying, we find that \\( \\theta = 36^\\circ \\)."
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 1786,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 1787,
        "char_start": 1597,
        "effective_step": 11,
        "end_token_index": 716,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 717,
        "step_number": 11,
        "text": "Step 11: Calculate \\( BM \\) using \\( \\theta = 36^\\circ \\):\n\\[ BM = \\frac{1}{\\sin 54^\\circ} = \\frac{1}{\\cos 36^\\circ} = \\frac{1}{\\frac{\\sqrt{5}+1}{4}} = \\frac{4}{\\sqrt{5}+1} = \\sqrt{5} - 1 \\]"
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 1914,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 1916,
        "char_start": 1789,
        "effective_step": 12,
        "end_token_index": 785,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 786,
        "step_number": 12,
        "text": "Step 12: Therefore, \\( AB = \\sqrt{11^2 + (\\sqrt{5} - 1)^2} = \\sqrt{121 + 6 - 2\\sqrt{5}} = \\sqrt{127 - 2\\sqrt{5}} \\approx 11 \\)."
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 2001,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 2003,
        "char_start": 1918,
        "effective_step": 13,
        "end_token_index": 819,
        "near_end": true,
        "prefix_token_count": 820,
        "step_number": 13,
        "text": "Step 13: The perimeter of triangle \\( ABC \\) is \\( 3 \\times AB = 3 \\times 11 = 33 \\)."
      }
    ]
